1986  the year a legend was born  it's one of the best performing  motorsport models ever  the idol of an entire generation  the first bmw m3  it can go anywhere  dirt road  or race track  the beamer m3 was designed in both  motorsports and road going models  under the hood was an optimized  four-cylinder engine that had already  scored successes for the bmw 1800 ti in  the 1960s  the j-sport company is based in cologne  normally its staff customize toyotas but  managing director gerald boning has a  personal attachment to the early beamer  m3s  what he loves about the m3 is for one  that it's a proper motorsports car and  shows it with its flared fenders and it  was the last car built for both purposes  nowadays all he sees is wannabe racing  cars or actual racing cars that only  vaguely resemble a production car  that's the attraction of the m3 it's  just as suitable for doing your shopping  on saturday as for driving a few laps on  the nurburgring these hours come  the earliest m3s were quite easy going  on regular roads its 215 horsepower  engine enabled top speeds of 245  kilometers an hour in the 1980s it  practically had the fast lane to itself  gerald bonango has a 1987 m3 in very  good condition  he describes it as a chicato replica dtm  car  johnny chacotto was also a grand prix  motorcycle champion and he's most  impressed that someone could race both  motorcycles and cars  the venezuelan star's first german  touring car's victory was in 1989 in an  m3  between 1987 and 1992 the m3 won two  european touring car championships two  german titles and several other  international competitions over 1500  victories with more than 50 championship  titles in seven years made the beamer m3  the world's top touring car  nowadays an m3 in pristine condition can  be had for around 30 000 euros the  engine may not have the best pickup at  lower revs but on the racetrack it more  than holds its own on city streets too  it's a faithful workhorse  the bmw m3 legend on the road and  racetrack

